"""
Production settings for {{ project_name }}.

This file contains production-ready security and performance configurations:
- DEBUG disabled
- PostgreSQL database
- Security middleware and settings
- Static file serving with WhiteNoise
- Comprehensive logging

REQUIRED ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES:
- SECRET_KEY: Django secret key (generate with: python -c 'from django.core.management.utils import get_random_secret_key; print(get_random_secret_key())')
- DATABASE_URL: Superuser PostgreSQL connection string; used for migrations (schema changes require elevated privileges)
- RUNTIME_DATABASE_URL: Restricted NOSUPERUSER/NOBYPASSRLS role connection string; required for runtime serving
- ALLOWED_HOSTS: Comma-separated list of allowed hostnames
- SENTRY_DSN: (optional) Sentry error tracking DSN

OPTIONAL ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES:
- REDIS_URL: When set, enables Redis as the shared cache backend (recommended; standard on Railway)
- USE_X_FORWARDED_FOR: Defaults to ``True`` in production; set to ``False`` for single-host
- TRUSTED_PROXY_COUNT: Defaults to ``1``; the number of reverse proxies in front of the app

COMMAND-MODE ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES (mutually exclusive, one-shot):
- QUICKSCALE_PRIVILEGED_COMMAND: Set by start.sh to ``migrate`` or ``createcachetable``
  to run privileged DB commands with the superuser ``DATABASE_URL``. Requires
  ``RUNTIME_DATABASE_URL=""`` (explicitly blank).
- QUICKSCALE_NON_DB_COMMAND: Set by the launcher to ``collectstatic`` or
  ``compilemessages`` to run DB-free bootstrap commands. Does not require
  a real database connection.
"""

